A||||3||Larry Moss||cheap performance?||||1||
Z||000000||Larry Moss||01-15-2001||05:04 PM||||Hi:<P>I am new to American cars and Fiero's.  I have an 87 GT with 204K.  THe car was not well maintained, but the engine is quite strong, although it burns about 1 quart per 150 - 200 mi.<P>I want to fix the problem without spending lots of money on an engine that has enough power.  What I was thinking was to have a ring job (I do not know the cost) and bolt on a modified head (from the Fiero store). Last, I would upgrade the coil to an MSW Blaster ss ($49.00) and switch to a high output cat converter. Is this idea reasonable, or would you suggest something else?<P>I do not race, but once a month I drive about 1200 miles over one weekend (at a constant 3500 rpm). <P>||||reg||1
Z||000001||StuGood||01-15-2001||06:44 PM||||For the oil consumption problem, I would suggest putting in new a set of valve stem seals, especially if it smokes on startup.  You don't have to pull the heads to do it.<P>1 quart every 150-200 miles sounds like more than valve seals, but it'd be worth a shot.  After that, the ring job sounds good - but with 200k+ miles, it's silly not to do a valve job, too.<P>A basic tuneup (including compression check) is the place to start - just like with any other engine - before you start modifying anything.  Good luck  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">!      ||||reg||1
Z||000002||Old Lar||01-15-2001||06:49 PM||||The last car that I had that went through that much oil in 200 miles needed an overhaul.  It may be just rings, but with 204K miles on it, it probably needs more. <BR>To put on a modified head will stress out the engine.  A high output cat will soon be fouled by all the oil burning.  Money wasted.<P>A 1200 mile trip = 6 quarts of oil!||||reg||3
Z||000003||DavidHenshaw||01-16-2001||11:33 AM||||Ouch! That's a lot of oil going through that engine. I have a 2.8 V6 with 210,000 miles which uses maybe a half quart in a nonstop 500 mile drive.<P>With the oil consumption you describe I would expect an engine overhaul is needed. Would include new bearings on the crank and of course new rubber seals front and rear. Rings, valves and valve guide seal replacement go without saying. Its a lot of work but its better than having the engine crash when you're 600 miles from home.<P>Dave<P>86 GT||||reg||1
